WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.304
Li Shimin ascended the throne as Emperor Taizong of Tang, determined to be a good emperor. He said: water can carry a boat, but it can also overturn it.

00:00:08.654 --> 00:00:12.686
He often reminded himself to listen to the voices of the people.

00:00:13.036 --> 00:00:19.036
He opened the channels for advice, encouraged his ministers to speak frankly, and never punished anyone for their words.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:23.994
The ministers said all they wished to say, and the mood at court was lively.

00:00:24.344 --> 00:00:33.344
He appointed talented people as officials, no matter their background. Fang Xuanling and Du Ruhui became the ministers he trusted most.

00:00:33.694 --> 00:00:37.342
The young scholars happily walked through the palace gate.

00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:46.092
He lightened the people's taxes and labor duties, so farmers could farm in peace, and every household had grain to spare.

00:00:46.442 --> 00:00:55.850
Under his rule, the Tang dynasty grew strong, and envoys from many lands came to court. Later generations called this period the Zhenguan Reign.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.232
The envoys marveled at the bustle and prosperity of Chang'an.

